    "version": "webp-usfx-2026-10-13-35a6adf626e5",
    "sourceBook": "ACT",
    "sourceChapter": 14,
    "sourceVerse": "15",
    "text": "“Men, why are you doing these things? We also are men of the same nature as you, and bring you good news, that you should turn from these vain things to the living God, who made the sky, the earth, the sea, and all that is in them;",
    "canonical": {
      "book": "ACT",
      "chapter": 14,
      "verse": 15
    },
    "alignment": "canonical-compatible",
    "textStatus": "present",
    "verification": "literal-source",
    "editorialReview": "unreviewed"
  },
  {
    "sourceId": "webp",
    "version": "webp-usfx-2026-10-13-35a6adf626e5",
    "sourceBook": "ACT",
    "sourceChapter": 18,
    "sourceVerse": "2",
    "text": "He found a certain Jew named Aquila, a man of Pontus by race, who had recently come from Italy with his wife Priscilla, because Claudius had commanded all the Jews to depart from Rome. He came to them,",
    "canonical": {
      "book": "ACT",
      "chapter": 18,
      "verse": 2
    },
    "alignment": "canonical-compatible",
    "textStatus": "present",
    "verification": "literal-source",
    "editorialReview": "unreviewed"
  },
  {
    "sourceId": "webp",
    "version": "webp-usfx-2026-10-13-35a6adf626e5",
    "sourceBook": "ACT",
    "sourceChapter": 18,
    "sourceVerse": "3",
    "text": "and because he practiced the same trade, he lived with them and worked, for by trade they were tent makers.",
    "canonical": {
      "book": "ACT",
      "chapter": 18,
      "verse": 3
    },
    "alignment": "canonical-compatible",
    "textStatus": "present",
    "verification": "literal-source",
    "editorialReview": "unreviewed"
  },
  {
    "sourceId": "webp",
    "version": "webp-usfx-2026-10-13-35a6adf626e5",
    "sourceBook": "ACT",
    "sourceChapter": 18,
    "sourceVerse": "4",
    "text": "He reasoned in the synagogue every Sabbath and persuaded Jews and Greeks.",
    "canonical": {
      "book": "ACT",
      "chapter": 18,
      "verse": 4
    },
    "alignment": "canonical-compatible",
    "textStatus": "present",
    "verification": "literal-source",
    "editorialReview": "unreviewed"
  },
  {
    "sourceId": "webp",
    "version": "webp-usfx-2026-10-13-35a6adf626e5",
    "sourceBook": "ACT",
    "sourceChapter": 18,
    "sourceVerse": "12",
    "text": "But when Gallio was proconsul of Achaia, the Jews with one accord rose up against Paul and brought him before the judgment seat,",
    "canonical": {
      "book": "ACT",
      "chapter": 18,
      "verse": 12
    },
    "alignment": "canonical-compatible",
    "textStatus": "present",
    "verification": "literal-source",
    "editorialReview": "unreviewed"
  },
  {
    "sourceId": "webp",
    "version": "webp-usfx-2026-10-13-35a6adf626e5",
    "sourceBook": "ACT",
    "sourceChapter": 18,
    "sourceVerse": "19",
    "text": "He came to Ephesus, and he left them there; but he himself entered into the synagogue and reasoned with the Jews.",
    "canonical": {
      "book": "ACT",
      "chapter": 18,
      "verse": 19
    },
    "alignment": "canonical-compatible",
    "textStatus": "present",
    "verification": "literal-source",
    "editorialReview": "unreviewed"
  },
  {
    "sourceId": "webp",
    "version": "webp-usfx-2026-10-13-35a6adf626e5",
    "sourceBook": "ACT",
    "sourceChapter": 18,
    "sourceVerse": "24",
    "text": "Now a certain Jew named Apollos, an Alexandrian by race, an eloquent man, came to Ephesus. He was mighty in the Scriptures.",
    "canonical": {
      "book": "ACT",
      "chapter": 18,
      "verse": 24
    },
    "alignment": "canonical-compatible",
    "textStatus": "present",
    "verification": "literal-source",
    "editorialReview": "unreviewed"
  },
  {
    "sourceId": "webp",
    "version": "webp-usfx-2026-10-13-35a6adf626e5",
    "sourceBook": "ACT",
    "sourceChapter": 18,
    "sourceVerse": "25",
    "text": "This man had been instructed in the way of the Lord; and being fervent in spirit, he spoke and taught accurately the things concerning Jesus, although he knew only the baptism of John.",
    "canonical": {
      "book": "ACT",
      "chapter": 18,
      "verse": 25
    },
    "alignment": "canonical-compatible",
    "textStatus": "present",
    "verification": "literal-source",
    "editorialReview": "unreviewed"
  },
  {
    "sourceId": "webp",
    "version": "webp-usfx-2026-10-13-35a6adf626e5",
    "sourceBook": "ACT",
    "sourceChapter": 18,
    "sourceVerse": "26",
    "text": "He began to speak boldly in the synagogue. But when Priscilla and Aquila heard him, they took him aside, and explained to him the way of God more accurately.",
    "canonical": {
      "book": "ACT",
      "chapter": 18,
      "verse": 26
    },
    "alignment": "canonical-compatible",
    "textStatus": "present",
    "verification": "literal-source",
    "editorialReview": "unreviewed"
  },
  {
    "sourceId": "webp",
    "version": "webp-usfx-2026-10-13-35a6adf626e5",
    "sourceBook": "ACT",
    "sourceChapter": 18,
    "sourceVerse": "27",
    "text": "When he had determined to pass over into Achaia, the brothers encouraged him; and wrote to the disciples to receive him. When he had come, he greatly helped those who had believed through grace;",
    "canonical": {
      "book": "ACT",
      "chapter": 18,
      "verse": 27
    },
    "alignment": "canonical-compatible",
    "textStatus": "present",
    "verification": "literal-source",
    "editorialReview": "unreviewed"
  },
  {
    "sourceId": "webp",
